one of the guys there, totally left wing, anti everything, and he's always talking against the rabbis,

c1005
01:10:13.820 --> 01:10:21.040
trying to impose their values on others, and then he comes and he protests,

c1006
01:10:21.220 --> 01:10:29.960
there are workers that come from Thailand, they come to Israel, and you know what they do?

c1007
01:10:29.960 --> 01:10:33.060
to eat dogs.

c1008
01:10:33.980 --> 01:10:36.860
And he wanted them to be prohibited.

c1009
01:10:37.380 --> 01:10:40.220
The most irrational thing to do in the world.

c1010
01:10:40.700 --> 01:10:42.060
To eat dogs.

c1011
01:10:44.140 --> 01:10:45.340
I have nothing against it.

c1012
01:10:46.040 --> 01:10:48.920
And we should not permit them to eat dogs.

c1013
01:10:50.120 --> 01:10:51.200
And he's talking about all this.

c1014
01:10:51.700 --> 01:10:52.300
And I would like to say,

c1015
01:10:52.540 --> 01:10:54.740
what about not eating pork?

c1016
01:10:54.740 --> 01:10:56.060
He would say, well, that is stupid.

c1017
01:10:56.600 --> 01:10:57.140
Why?

c1018
01:10:57.140 --> 01:11:05.780
because he accepts the goal taboo but doesn't accept the Jewish table got the

c1019
01:11:05.780 --> 01:11:15.080
point all right all right any other question you had a question

c1020
01:11:27.140 --> 01:11:32.860
Therefore, to me, to the word of God, or detract from it,

c1021
01:11:34.100 --> 01:11:38.140
like God says you shall kill a criminal who is convicted,

c1022
01:11:38.140 --> 01:11:41.100
and then you have a sanhedrin who says, no, you should not,

c1023
01:11:41.260 --> 01:11:43.420
even though it is said you are not going to do it.

c1024
01:11:44.420 --> 01:11:50.020
And then you see the diametrically opposed result to the extent of...

c1025
01:11:50.020 --> 01:11:51.320
I have a problem.

c1026
01:11:51.320 --> 01:11:55.000
First of all, hello?

c1027
01:11:56.040 --> 01:12:05.000
We disagree on many things, but you know that sometimes there is more affection about people who disagree than about people who agree.

c1028
01:12:05.420 --> 01:12:13.940
So I'm going to confess, when I came here today, I was hoping that he should be present.

c1029
01:12:14.420 --> 01:12:14.700
All right?

c1030
01:12:14.780 --> 01:12:16.660
I was hoping that he should be present.

c1031
01:12:16.660 --> 01:12:20.660
So I welcome the question, and I welcome the question because it's a good question.

c1032
01:12:20.660 --> 01:12:23.320
and it gives you opportunity to explain more.

c1033
01:12:26.140 --> 01:12:26.860
Lay mental.

c1034
01:12:29.160 --> 01:12:30.740
The Tora is the lay mental of Israel.

c1035
01:12:31.180 --> 01:12:31.840
The mental law.

c1036
01:12:32.420 --> 01:12:32.960
Listen to this.

c1037
01:12:35.140 --> 01:12:36.500
I, the first person,

c1038
01:12:37.360 --> 01:12:41.080
speaking to this wonderful lady, second person, all right?

c1039
01:12:41.720 --> 01:12:42.880
I say a word.

c1040
01:12:43.520 --> 01:12:45.280
I have something, a meaning in my head.

c1041
01:12:47.280 --> 01:12:49.640
But my word means nothing

c1042
01:12:49.640 --> 01:12:56.680
until she processed this word according to her mind.

c1043
01:12:58.700 --> 01:13:02.220
The meaning is not what I have in my mind,

c1044
01:13:02.220 --> 01:13:04.120
because once that I speak it,

c1045
01:13:04.600 --> 01:13:08.880
I address it, say to Mr. Ben-Harrosh,

c1046
01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:13.600
and now the meaning of the word is

c1047
01:13:13.600 --> 01:13:19.620
according to what the mind of Ben Arosh would process it.

c1048
01:13:20.380 --> 01:13:23.940
Now, if I instead of speaking to Mr. Ben Arosh,

c1049
01:13:24.000 --> 01:13:27.240
I would be talking to somebody from Finland

c1050
01:13:27.240 --> 01:13:30.240
with a different kind of background.

c1051
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:32.700
He may take the same word

c1052
01:13:32.700 --> 01:13:36.420
and understand it differently

c1053
01:13:36.420 --> 01:13:38.020
because his mind is differently.

c1054
01:13:40.300 --> 01:13:42.360
God spoke the Tora

c1055
01:13:42.360 --> 01:13:46.180
not to the Aztecs.

c1056
01:13:46.500 --> 01:13:47.680
I'm talking about the homage.

c1057
01:13:48.040 --> 01:13:49.280
Maybe he gave another Tora to them.

c1058
01:13:49.540 --> 01:13:53.300
The homage, the message that God gave in Sinai.

c1059
01:13:54.440 --> 01:13:56.320
It was to us.

c1060
01:13:57.840 --> 01:14:03.140
And it depends on the way we, our mind, process this message.

c1061
01:14:04.480 --> 01:14:05.760
When God says,

c1062
01:14:05.760 --> 01:14:07.320
Ukshatam leotayadecha.

c1063
01:14:08.660 --> 01:14:11.060
For whatever reason, I don't care why.

c1064
01:14:11.060 --> 01:14:12.760
our mind processed this

c1065
01:14:12.760 --> 01:14:15.120
to Mr. Filin

c1066
01:14:15.120 --> 01:14:18.940
and that is the meaning of it

c1067
01:14:18.940 --> 01:14:21.140
because he spoke to us

c1068
01:14:21.140 --> 01:14:23.220
and that is the way

c1069
01:14:23.220 --> 01:14:24.620
we understood it

c1070
01:14:24.620 --> 01:14:26.960
and if we

c1071
01:14:26.960 --> 01:14:28.140
made a mistake

c1072
01:14:28.140 --> 01:14:30.900
nobody could tell us that he made a mistake

c1073
01:14:30.900 --> 01:14:33.860
because he didn't speak to Mr. A, B, C, D, E

c1074
01:14:33.860 --> 01:14:36.020
he spoke to us

c1075
01:14:36.020 --> 01:14:37.620
and that is the way

c1076
01:14:37.620 --> 01:14:39.080
we understood it

c1077
01:14:39.080 --> 01:14:47.580
And hasri shalom, if there is an error, then we pray to God, He knows our mind, He is the great communicator,

c1078
01:14:47.580 --> 01:14:56.080
He knows what terms to convey in order to deliver whatever message, He knows exactly our mind.

c1079
01:14:56.080 --> 01:15:01.580
So if He knew that uksharta amlota l'arecha, we are going to understand a tefillin,

c1080
01:15:01.580 --> 01:15:08.580
and instead of tefillin He wanted us to wear a bathing suit, He should have to choose a different term.

c1081
01:15:08.580 --> 01:15:14.660
He chose ukshatam leotarecha because he knew that for us ukshatam leotarecha means to put on tefillin.

c1082
01:15:16.100 --> 01:15:20.520
And therefore, by virtue of giving the Tora to us,

c1083
01:15:23.260 --> 01:15:26.500
the act of giving the Tora creates already Tora shebealpe.

c1084
01:15:26.760 --> 01:15:31.460
Once that you give the text, once that you issue this word out of your mouth,

c1085
01:15:32.480 --> 01:15:35.780
the word is no longer yours, it belongs to the second person.

c1086
01:15:35.780 --> 01:15:38.540
The way that second person understands it.

c1087
01:15:38.580 --> 01:15:41.360
and that is the meaning of the Tora

c1088
01:15:41.360 --> 01:15:44.280
you think that the text

c1089
01:15:44.280 --> 01:15:46.240
he didn't speak to you

c1090
01:15:46.240 --> 01:15:49.140
he spoke to the Jewish people

c1091
01:15:49.140 --> 01:15:52.160
Mr. Christian

c1092
01:15:52.160 --> 01:15:53.900
Mr. Buddhist

c1093
01:15:53.900 --> 01:15:54.920
Mr. Muslim

c1094
01:15:54.920 --> 01:15:57.060
he did not speak to you

c1095
01:15:57.060 --> 01:15:59.660
he spoke to us

c1096
01:15:59.660 --> 01:16:02.200
that is the way we understood it

c1097
01:16:02.200 --> 01:16:04.040
that is our lament time

c1098
01:16:04.040 --> 01:16:08.860
End of discussion

c1099
01:16:08.860 --> 01:16:10.300
The Tora says

c1100
01:16:10.300 --> 01:16:10.980
Zabachta

c1101
01:16:10.980 --> 01:16:12.040
slaughter

c1102
01:16:12.040 --> 01:16:17.180
How does it mean slaughter?

c1103
01:16:17.920 --> 01:16:18.660
We understand

c1104
01:16:18.660 --> 01:16:20.580
that it doesn't have to be a pegan

c1105
01:16:20.580 --> 01:16:22.400
that it will be slaughtered

c1106
01:16:22.400 --> 01:16:23.900
That is the way we understood it

c1107
01:16:23.900 --> 01:16:26.380
If God didn't want it

c1108
01:16:26.380 --> 01:16:28.040
